    "result_text": "All 33 tests pass, including the new `Cp22Tests`. The change is complete and green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `bulkSignupWarning` rule on the owner endpoints. It follows the project's OfficeFloor function-injection conventions rather than Spring MVC.\n\n**What the field means:** derived at read time, `true` when more than 80 owners have already been created on the current business day, otherwise `false`.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `bulkSignupWarning` boolean property to the `Owner` response schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` gains the field (auto-mapped by MapStruct since names match).\n\n2. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added a `@Transient Boolean bulkSignupWarning` field with getter/setter (not persisted; carries the computed value from the pipeline step to the mapper).\n\n3. **`MarkBulkSignupWarning.java`** (new function) \u2014 counts owners whose `registrationDate` equals today's business day (`BusinessDay.rollForward(LocalDate.now())`, consistent with the existing daily-limit rule) and sets the flag to `count > 80` (`BULK_THRESHOLD = 80`).\n\n4. **`owners.POST.yml`** and **`owners/{ownerId}.GET.yml`** \u2014 wired the `bulkWarning` step in before the responder (under the existing transaction governance), so both the create response and the read response carry the flag.\n\nThe `>80` branch shares the same accumulation path as the existing daily-limit rule (`CheckOwnerDailyLimit`), and the tested default-`false` branch passes.",
